meta_description:
7,241 likes, 108 comments - chrisburkard on October 21, 2026: "During our trip to Kamchatka in 2012 we foud board-snapping waves, argued with Russian soldiers, and watched locals shoot firearms seemingly at random into the dunes, but what really made us question our safety was the transportation. From Soviet-era MI8 choppers that seemed to operate more on the stubbornness of their pilots and a helping of elbow grease to old troop carrier trucks that could somehow still hold a terrifyingly fast pace through overgrown forest roads, it felt like we’d been transported back to a time before safety regulations or sanity. This sense turned out to be fairly representative of the whole adventure. We scored waves that wouldn’t have been out of place on any latitude  coast, but had likely never seen a surfboard on their face. We fished for food alongside men who were doing the same - and would continue to do so long after we returned to our western cocoon of comfort and convenience. The whole time we were watched over by looming volcanoes, to which we were just a tiny blip in the 50,000 years of life that had unfolded beneath them. It was a surreal adventure coming to this place out of time, and I think it’s fair to say it gave all six of us a more well-rounded outlook on life.
@cyrus_sutton @danedamus @benweiland @tearevor @keithmalloy_bimarianfilms 

Shot on assignment for @surfer_magazine".

